==Interrogatives==
*{{Lang|cbw|Sin-o?}} Who?
*{{Lang|cbw|Kanin-o?}} To whom?
*{{Lang|cbw|Uno?}} What?
*{{Lang|cbw|Giuno?}} How? (past)
*{{Lang|cbw|Unhon/unohon?}} How? (future)
*{{Lang|cbw|Haman?}} Where? (for person or object)
*{{Lang|cbw|Ngain?}} Where? (for place)
*{{Lang|cbw|Diin?}} Where? (for directions or origin)
*{{Lang|cbw|Kanus-a?}} When?
*{{Lang|cbw|Ngaman?}} Why?
*{{Lang|cbw|Amo baja?}} Really?
*{{Lang|cbw|Tagpila?}} How much?

{{Lang|cbw|Haman}}, {{Lang|cbw|ngain}}, and {{Lang|cbw|diin}} mean 'where'. They have distinct uses in Kabalianon.

{{Lang|cbw|Haman}} is used when asking about a person or object.

*{{Lang|cbw|Haman si Papa?}} (Where is Papa?)
*{{Lang|cbw|Haman gibutang an gunting?}} (Where was the scissor put?)

{{Lang|cbw|Ngain}} is used when asking about a place.
*{{Lang|cbw|Ngain man (ki)ta mularga?}} (Where are we going to?)
*{{Lang|cbw|Ngain man kaw pasingud?}} (Where are you going?)

{{Lang|cbw|Diin}} is used when asking about directions or origin.
*{{Lang|cbw|Diin man ini dapita?}} (Where is this place?)
*{{Lang|cbw|Taga Diin man kaw?}} (Where are you from?)
*{{Lang|cbw|Diin man kaw gikan?}} (Where were you?)

